\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Conclusion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The most impactful architectural decision is 
\f0\b using 
\f5\fs26 \strokec2 import_bulk(on_duplicate="update")
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  with deterministic 
\f5\fs26 \strokec2 _key
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  values
\f1\b0  rather than AQL UPSERT \'97 this single choice determines whether initial seeding takes hours or weeks. The second critical insight is that 
\f0\b every source in this stack supports some form of incremental update detection
\f1\b0 , eliminating the need for full re-ingestion after the initial seed. OSV's 
\f2\fs26 modified_id.csv
\f1\fs24 , NVD's 
\f2\fs26 lastModStartDate
\f1\fs24 , and git-based diff detection for ATT&CK/Nuclei/ExploitDB collectively enable a system that processes only deltas, keeping the knowledge graph current with minimal API calls and compute overhead. The plugin-based agent architecture with YAML configuration makes adding new sources a matter of implementing four methods against a well-defined interface, while 
\f2\fs26 TopologicalSorter
\f1\fs24  ensures CWE loads before NVD, ATT&CK before CAPEC, and 800-53 before SCF \'97 without manual coordination.\
